record('khyati-pmjay-claims','PM-JAY → Khyati: claim earnings, clinical allegations and later bail','Public health cover reaches a named private hospital. A sessions-court account records ₹16.64 crore in PM-JAY claim earnings and alleges ₹8 crore bank-loan use; patient-level records and bank reconciliation remain absent. The clinical charges are contested. The Supreme Court granted the chairman bail in December2025; discharge refusals were reported in May2026.',ks,['mohfw','pmjay-gujarat','khyati-hospital','ahmedabad-bariatrics','kartik-patel','khyati-case','supreme-court'],['mohfw-pmjay','pmjay-khyati','operator-khyati','kartik-operator','khyati-proceeding','sc-kartik-bail'],kd,['funding','services','welfare','legal','review'],'Claims31Mar2022–11Nov2024; clinical incident11Nov2024; last retained procedural report9May2026','Dr Prashant Vazirani’s counsel argued clinical indications and pre-authorisation justified the procedures, complications could explain the deaths, and some patients declined treatment. Kartik Patel’s counsel disputed personal withdrawal and day-to-day management. The Gujarat HC rejected the doctor’s May2025 bail plea on a prima facie view; the Supreme Court’s 11Dec2025 order records later bail for him and all other co-accused and grants Patel bail. A May2026 report records discharge refusal. No final conviction or acquittal is established.',['Legitimate PM-JAY treatment also earns package revenue; the total cannot be classified as fraud without claim-level findings.','A corporate loan repayment can serve hospital operations. It does not establish personal withdrawal or illegality without the source-of-funds and clinical evidence.','Adverse medical outcome alone does not prove unnecessary treatment or criminal intent.'],'Obtain authenticated claims adjudication and disbursement ledgers, clinical videos/independent reviews, bank-use tracing and the final reasoned trial or appellate judgment; reconcile each disputed claim and preserve any acquittal or recovery.',kamount,'alleged','Charges contested; chairman granted bail 11Dec2025; discharge refusals reported May2026; no merits verdict retained','2026-05-09','2022-03-31','2026-05-09',kg,['The ₹8 crore account and ₹16.64 crore earnings may overlap; do not add them or infer a residual.','No hospital-specific government recovery, final loss, bank identity or amount paid to individual patients is established.','A general national anti-fraud response is included as policy context, not as an answer clearing this hospital.'])

