record('byju-credit-bcci','Byju’s: a dollar loan, an Indian guarantee and a ₹158 crore escrow','The source trail links US lender funding through GLAS to BYJU’S Alpha, Think & Learn’s guarantee and a separate BCCI sponsorship debt. The Supreme Court set aside approval of the ₹158 crore settlement because insolvency-withdrawal procedures were bypassed, while expressly declining a merits finding on stakeholder conduct. The August2026 NCLAT dismissal also left the underlying creditor dispute open.',bs,['glas','byju-alpha','think-learn','bcci','riju-ravindran','byju-coc','nclat','supreme-court'],['glas-alpha-credit','think-alpha-parent','think-glas-guarantee','think-bcci-sponsorship','riju-bcci-settlement','bcci-coc-escrow','nclat-glas-procedure'],bd,['funding','organisations','legal','review'],'Facility24Nov2021; CIRP admitted16Jul2024; SC23Oct2024; NCLAT17Aug2026','Riju Ravindran’s undertaking said settlement funds were personal, derived from his share-sale resources, and did not come from the disputed US loan proceeds. GLAS challenged that provenance and priority. The Supreme Court §§86–87 made no finding on stakeholder conduct and left remedies under the proper withdrawal procedure available. In2026 Byju’s side challenged lender authorisations and claim quantum; NCLAT declined to adjudicate those merits in an appeal from a listing order.',['A documented guarantee and operational debt explain a multi-creditor insolvency without themselves proving diversion.','Payment by a third party can be lawful; lawful source and compliance still need proof where challenged.','The US transfer disputes and Indian withdrawal litigation are distinct proceedings; one cannot stand in for a final outcome in the other.'],'Produce the relevant authenticated lender authorisations, disbursement/transfer bank records, guarantee enforcement and final merits orders; determine the exact funds used for settlement and any later escrow distribution.',bamount,'documented','Indian settlement approval set aside; funds protected in escrow by order; August2026 procedural appeal dismissed, underlying issues left open','2026-08-17','2021-11-24','2026-08-17',bg,['Dollar loan principal and rupee operational-debt settlement are different currencies and obligations; never sum them.','No final US recovery or damages number is presented, and no inference about public subsidy or school-delivery outcome is supported.','No current company valuation is supplied merely because the brand was previously described as a unicorn.'])

