record('nsap-davp-earmarking','NSAP → DAVP: publicity spending and missing work confirmation','CAG traced two approved publicity amounts into DAVP work orders, then found₹2.83crore charged to NSAP for other ministry schemes and paid before confirmation of execution. That documents an earmarking and delivery-verification failure. It does not prove partisan advertising or identify personal enrichment. Later parliamentary material checked here does not close this specific audit paragraph.',ns,['mord','nsap-iec','davp','pmay-ddu-publicity'],['mord-nsap-iec','mord-davp-orders','nsap-davp-paid','davp-other-schemes'],nd,['funding','procurement','welfare','services','review'],'June/August2017 sanctions; June/September2017 work orders; December2022 Ministry response; report8Aug2023','The Ministry told CAG in December2022 that it had taken the matter up with its IEC division. The2Apr2026 parliamentary action-taken report was also reviewed, but concerns recommendations of the Committee’s9threport and does not establish reconciliation, delivered-media receipts or recovery for CAG§5.5.1. This absence is not proof that no action exists elsewhere.',['Cross-scheme awareness can serve a legitimate public purpose; it still needs a lawful expenditure head and proof of delivery.','An accounting correction or subsequently supplied execution certificate could narrow or resolve the historical observation.'],'Produce the contemporaneous approved head-change, DAVP invoice and campaign execution certificates, payment ledger and a paragraph-specific accepted action-taken/recovery record.',namount,'documented','CAG finding with Ministry response; final paragraph-specific reconciliation or recovery not established','2023-08-08',None,None,ng,['The two sanctions and rounded₹2.83crore expenditure describe overlapping stages; never sum them.','This deep case re-examines the existing welfare-research:nsap-publicity finding. It is not a second independent incident or additional loss.','Government-agency payee is identified, but no media subcontractor or individual beneficiary is named by the cited paragraph.'])

